# Production deploy trigger

If the user says **deploy**, **prod deploy**, **deploy it**, **trigger deploy**,
**trigger deploy workflow**, or clear equivalents, treat that as authorization to
cut and push a production release tag from `main`.

Follow the **Production deploy (AI agents)** section in repository-root `AGENTS.md`
(canonical and **self-contained** — do not require gitignored `automation/`).

Summary:

1. Work must be on branch `main` in `unlockedventures/unlocked-ventures`.
2. Next annotated tag: `prod-YYYY.MM.N` (N increments within the month).
3. `-m` message: one short line summarizing recent `main` commits
   (`git log -5 --oneline`, or since the previous `prod-*` tag when present).
4. `git tag -a prod-… -m "…"` then `git push origin refs/tags/prod-…`.
5. That tag push starts **Deploy IONOS**. Do not rely on pushing `main` alone.

Keep packaging in Dockerfiles, compose, `.github/` only — not `src/`.
Do not put deploy secrets or media archives in tracked files.
Reuse VPS bind mounts `/var/lib/unlocked-venture` (Postgres) and
`/var/lib/unlocked-venture/media` — never wipe/re-import on a normal tag deploy.
Optional local ops notes may live under gitignored `automation/` when present.
